{
    desc => '2p pastes 2 copies of yanked text below',
    description => <<'END_DESC',
Macro: `xt/visual/macros/paste_2p`

Tests `yy` followed by `2p` which yanks the current line then pastes
2 copies below it.

**initial.png** — Two lines of text. Cursor at line 1 col 0.

Keys: `yy` then `2p`

**after_yank.png** — Intermediate state: line 1 yanked into register.

**after_2p.png** — Line 1 (`first line`) is duplicated twice below.
Buffer now has 4 lines: `first line`, `first line`, `first line`, `second line`.
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('yy');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_yank');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('2p');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_2p');
    },
}
__DATA__
first line
second line
